.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-EDITORS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-editors ,
.Nm awk ,
.Nm cmp ,
.Nm diff ,
.Nm ed ,
.Nm patch ,
.Nm sed ,
.Nm vi
.Nd BusyBox editors and text filters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm awk
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Op Ar AWK_PROGRAM
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Nm cmp
.Op Fl ls
.Op Fl n Ar NUM
.Ar FILE1
.Op Ar FILE2 Op Ar SKIP1 Op Ar SKIP2
.Nm diff
.Op Fl abBdiNqrTstw
.Op Fl L Ar LABEL
.Op Fl S Ar FILE
.Op Fl U Ar LINES
.Ar FILE1 FILE2
.Nm ed
.Op Fl p Ar PROMPT
.Op Fl s
.Op Ar FILE
.Nm patch
.Op Fl RNE
.Op Fl p Ar N
.Op Fl i Ar DIFF
.Op Ar ORIGFILE Op Ar PATCHFILE
.Nm sed
.Op Fl i Ns Op Ar SFX
.Op Fl nrE
.Op Fl f Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Op Fl e Ar CMD
.Ar ...
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Nm sed
.Op Fl i Ns Op Ar SFX
.Op Fl nrE
.Ar CMD
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Nm vi
.Op Fl c Ar CMD
.Op Fl R
.Op Fl H
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the editor and text filter applets of BusyBox 1.36.1
as built for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width patch
.It Nm awk
Process input files with an awk program.
.It Nm cmp
Compare
.Ar FILE1
with
.Ar FILE2 ,
or with standard input if the second file is omitted.
.It Nm diff
Compare files line by line and print their differences.
Only unified diff output is supported.
.It Nm ed
Edit text a line at a time.
.It Nm patch
Apply changes from a patch file.
.It Nm sed
Execute editing commands on input files and write to standard output,
or edit files in place with
.Fl i .
If no
.Fl e
or
.Fl f
is given, the first non-option argument is the command string;
remaining arguments are input files, or standard input if none are given.
.It Nm vi
Edit files on a terminal.
It requires raw terminal mode, which the Rach2 console and
pseudoterminal slaves provide.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss awk
.Bl -tag -width "-e AWK_PROGRAM"
.It Fl v Ar VAR=VAL
Set a variable.
.It Fl F Ar SEP
Set the field separator.
.It Fl f Ar FILE
Read the program from a file.
.It Fl e Ar AWK_PROGRAM
Supply the program as an argument.
.El
.Ss cmp
.Bl -tag -width "-n NUM"
.It Fl l
Print the decimal byte number and octal values of every differing byte.
.It Fl s
Suppress output.
.It Fl n Ar NUM
Compare at most this many bytes.
.El
.Ss diff
.Bl -tag -width "-L LABEL"
.It Fl a
Treat all files as text.
.It Fl b
Ignore changes in the amount of white space.
.It Fl B
Ignore changes consisting entirely of blank lines.
.It Fl d
Try to find a smaller set of changes.
.It Fl i
Ignore case differences.
.It Fl L Ar LABEL
Use the label instead of the file name in the unified diff header.
.It Fl N
Treat absent files as empty.
.It Fl q
Print only whether files differ.
.It Fl r
Recurse into directories.
.It Fl S Ar FILE
Start at this file when comparing directories.
.It Fl T
Prefix a tab when needed to align tabs.
.It Fl s
Report identical files.
.It Fl t
Expand tabs to spaces in output.
.It Fl U Ar LINES
Print this many lines of context.
.It Fl w
Ignore all white space.
.El
.Ss patch
.Bl -tag -width "--dry-run"
.It Fl p Ar N
Strip this many leading file name components.
.It Fl i Ar DIFF
Read the patch from this file instead of standard input.
.It Fl R
Reverse the patch.
.It Fl N
Ignore patches already applied.
.It Fl E
Remove output files that become empty.
.It Fl -dry-run
Do not change files.
.El
.Ss sed
.Bl -tag -width "-i[SFX]"
.It Fl e Ar CMD
Add a command to execute.
.It Fl f Ar FILE
Add the file's contents to the commands to execute.
.It Fl i Ns Op Ar SFX
Edit files in place.
If a suffix is given, append it to the names of backup files.
.It Fl n
Suppress automatic printing of the pattern space.
.It Fl r , Fl E
Use extended regular expressions.
.El
.Ss vi
.Bl -tag -width "-c CMD"
.It Fl c Ar CMD
Run an initial command.
Initial commands may also be supplied through
.Ev EXINIT
and
.Pa ~/.exrc .
.It Fl R
Read-only mode.
.It Fl H
List available features.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl echo foo | sed -e 's/f[a-zA-Z]o/bar/g'
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr console 4
